phasmaphobia the early access horror  game has taken twitch and social media  by storm  for those uninitiated phasmaphobia's  goal is simple though  achieving it is a little tricky you  either alone or with a group of friends  play a ghost hunter investigating a  haunting and trying to determine which  type of ghost you're dealing with  as you explore the area you will need to  use a variety of tools to gather  evidence before the ghost  kills you aside from the scares and this  the most horrific thing about  phasmaphobia in its current state is the  lackluster tutorial  it teaches you the basics for a few  investigation tools but leaves a lot for  you to figure out on your own  so with that in mind let's go over what  you need to know about phasmophobia  [Music]  i can hear it i can hear it  [Music]  as i mentioned before your job is to  figure out what kind of ghost you're  dealing with to do that you need to  first  identify which part of the building the  ghost is haunting and then you need to  find three separate pieces of hard  evidence to log in your journal  once you've found three clues you can  select the ghost in your journal and  gtfo  i like to imagine the ghostbusters roll  through after you catch the ghost but  i'll save that for when i start writing  my phasmaphobia fan fiction  what happened are you okay he slimed me  that's great  actual physical contact in order to find  evidence you need to know how the tools  work and how to use them effectively so  let's run through your gear  the emf reader is one of the most  important pieces of tech in your tool  kit  turn it on as you explore the house and  monitor the levels on it while clearing  rooms  high emf readings don't necessarily mean  danger or high levels of paranormal  activity it simply means that a ghost  could be nearby or that you could be in  the haunted room the emf reader is very  useful early on as it can help you  pinpoint which room is the source of  paranormal activity  if the emf reader hits level 5 you can  log that as evidence in your journal  when you have a minute to breathe  the spirit box is one of the creepiest  tools in the game as it often requires  you to sit in a room by yourself with  the lights off and try to have a  conversation with the ghost using your  real world microphone  i recommend saving spirit box duty for  the last person in your group that loads  in  aka your friend without the ssd with the  spirit box your goal is to get the ghost  to respond to you directly you can do  this by asking questions such as how old  are you can you speak to me is there  anything with me and so on the ghost can  respond to your questions in one of two  ways it can interact with the  environment like turning off lights or  moving objects or it can respond  directly through the spirit box  if you hear it through the spirit box  then you can mark that down as a clue in  your journal if it moves an object that  means that the spirit is nearby but that  doesn't count as a clue you can log in  the journal  alternatively the spirit box may just  say nothing detected in which case you  should try a different room  if you don't get nothing detected but  haven't heard a voice keep talking  keep in mind that for the spirit box to  work the lights need to be turned off  and some ghosts will only respond to you  if you're alone  if you do end up with the spirit box  make sure you're holding down proximity  chat when you talk  technically the ghost can hear your mic  inputs even if you don't push to talk  but i recommend doing it anyway just in  [Music]  case  i consider the video camera a stage two  item since you can only carry three  tools at once flashlight included i'd  leave the camera in the van until you've  pinpointed the haunted room  once you know where the paranormal  activity originated from return to the  van and grab the video camera  the bigger black camera place the camera  in a corner of the room that will give  you the widest feel of view possible you  can hold left click to rotate the camera  right click to turn it on and  f to place it don't forget to turn it on  before you bail  the last thing you want is to walk all  the way back to the van only to find out  that you didn't turn on the camera oddly  enough in phasmaphobia the green light  means recording and the red means off so  make sure to check  after you've placed the camera you or a  crew member should return to the van and  look at the monitor  left clicking on the in-game mouse will  change the cameras and clicking on the  keyboard will toggle night vision  whoever is monitoring the cameras should  be looking for ghost orbs  ghost orbs look like fireflies that  flutter by the camera if you see an orb  make sure to log it in your journal as a  clue  if you don't see one it's usually good  to try another angle just to be thorough  alternatively you can purchase head  mounted cameras which don't take up an  inventory slot and function similarly to  the camera  like the camera the ghostwriting book is  a stage 2 item  once you know which room the ghost is  camping out in set up the journal and  wait  if writing appears on the book mark it  in your journal when you have the  journal make sure to press  f to place it and not g to throw it down  technically the ghost can write in the  journal no matter how it's positioned  but i like to keep it facing up so my  crew can clearly see the book and the  best way to do this is placing it with  f apparently the ghost can even write in  the journal while you're holding it but  i haven't witnessed that yet  the galaxy brain play here is to set up  the journal in the view of your video  camera so you can see it from the  comfort of the van  the uv flashlight isn't what you're  probably thinking instead of using it to  find mucky business you'll use it to  spot fingerprints  like the last few gadgets you can  probably leave the uv flashlight in the  van during the early stages of the job  typically fingerprints don't appear  until later once there's been a  significant amount of paranormal  activity grab the uv flashlight and  sweep the affected  areas the best places to find hand and  fingerprints are on doors and windows if  you see something snap a picture for  extra cash and mark it in your journal  the thermometer is the only tool that  isn't part of your default tool kit i  highly recommend bringing one of these  along no matter the job  this is a great tool to use for the  initial sweep of the house  if you see the temperature drop below 10  there's a good chance you are in the  affected room  if it drops below zero then you'll want  to add freezing temperatures to your  journal  if you forget a thermometer which will  almost certainly happen you can tell if  a room is freezing  if you can see your breath admittedly  the thermometer makes things a bit too  easy on smaller maps as it can be a  dead giveaway as to which room is  haunted on bigger maps though the  thermometer can save you a ton of time  while those are the most important tools  you use on any given job there are a  handful of other optional tools that you  can take with you  these include a crucifix which can  protect you from certain ghosts  smudge sticks which can calm a ghost and  sound sensors which can help you  pinpoint the ghost location  while those tools can help you gather  evidence they aren't as straightforward  as the tools i listed  if you're new to phasmaphobia i  recommend sticking with the tools i  discussed earlier and slowly trying out  new ones as you get more comfortable  with the basics  it's also worth noting that if you  successfully use some of these optional  tools you can make a little extra cash  when you finish the job  now that we've run through some basic  equipment let's get into some best  practices for when you're out in the  field  first i highly recommend using in-game  voice chat once you and your team have  found your footing discord is nice when  you're starting out but it makes things  a bit too easy and  far less terrifying  the game also does some fun things with  audio implementation that make the  experience more immersive intense  for in-game communication use v for  proximity chat and b for global chat  courtesy of the handy walkie-talkie  keep in mind that your walkie-talkie  isn't always super reliable though  during high paranormal activity your  signal could get scrambled  if you aren't near your crew you'll have  no idea what could be happening to them  you can check paranormal activity levels  from the monitor in your van  usually it's good to let your team know  if there are any spikes low amounts of  activity could mean flickering lights or  moving objects  moderate spikes could mean direct  contact with the ghost and level 10  spikes usually mean the ghost  is hunting was this this opened for half  a second closed  oh right here i could hear him oh god  the best thing you can do for them is to  pray if a level 10 spike just occurred  and someone sanity percentage is  replaced by a question mark it means  they're dead  and if you're using in-game chat dead  team members can't communicate with you  if you're in the house during a level 10  spike your flashlight will start to  flicker  the front door will lock and you may see  the ghost appear and disappear  if the ghost is weak to crucifixes you  can stop it from hunting by throwing it  on the ground  or at the ghost if not hide in another  room turn off the lights and stay quiet  closets do nicely for this if you're  dealing with a shy ghost you can try  using its name as well  typically ghosts will get more annoyed  the more you say it  before you head into the house check the  whiteboard in the van to see the ghost  name  and if it responds to everyone or just  those who are alone  with each paranormal activity you  witness your sanity will drop you can  monitor your sanity in the  truck the lower it goes the easier it is  for a ghost to target you  you can regain your sanity by using  sanity pills which are available to  purchase before a job  as you complete jobs earn money and  level up you'll unlock new maps and gear  to test out  any additional gear you purchase and  take into the field can be lost if you  die  so be extra careful if you want to hold  on to those thermometers and motion  sensors  you do get an insurance payout though so  it's not a complete loss  the bigger maps like the high school and  asylum may also force you to change up  your tactics  the best way to go about these jobs is  to split into groups and clear rooms  methodically  study the map in the van before you  leave come up with a game plan  and designate a regroup point for your  team if someone gets lost you can check  their location via the map in the van  and guide them to safety using the  walkie-talkie  sanity pills are typically a must on  these maps as they usually take much  longer than most house jobs  when you find the affected room leave a  glow stick outside the door or have  someone make a mental note of it on the  map in the van  there are also some cases where you  won't be able to find the third piece of  evidence no matter how hard you try  if you're really struggling you can  check the ghost descriptions in your  journal  this isn't always the most accurate way  to solve a case but if you're low on  supplies there's no harm in checking the  journal to see if there are any familiar  patterns  there you have it almost everything you  need to know about hunting ghosts and  phasmaphobia  if there's something i missed please  leave it in the comments below to help  out your fellow ghost hunters  and with that good luck out there  you

